larly to Aux sends, at -Inf dB and post-fader.\n\nCrucially, on Auxiliary channels and Main LR, Route 32 reflects unity gain, aligning with master fader behavior. This confirms the initial hypothesis about the role of the master fader and reveals the defaults: Groups at 0 dB, Aux/LR at -Inf dB, and the channel fader at 0 dB. These differing settings point to intended routing differences.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"$bytes = [System.IO.File]::ReadAllBytes(\\\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\Allen & Heath\\\\SQ MixPad 1.6.1\\\\SQ MixPad.exe\\\")\\n$text = [System.Text.Encoding]::ASCII.GetString($bytes, 0x268600, 0x100000)\\n$idx = 0\\nwhile (($idx = $text.IndexOf(\\\"UnitsHelper\\\", $idx)) -ge 0) {\\n    $raw = 0x268600 + $idx\\n    $sub = $text.Substring([Math]::Max(0, $idx - 100), 300) -replace \\\"[^\\\\x20-\\\\x7E]+\\\", \\\" | \\\"\\n    Write-Host (\\\"0x{0:X6}: {1}\\\" -f $raw, $sub)\\n    $idx += 11\\n}\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolSummary":"\"Find UnitsHelper strings in SQ MixPad.exe\""}}]}
